  "id": "electronics.analog-circuits.power-amplifiers",
  "name": "Power Amplifiers",
  "level": "process",
  "parent": "electronics.analog-circuits",
  "description": "Design pedagogy for amplifiers that deliver watts to a load (speaker, antenna, motor) rather than millivolts of signal: class A (single device, linear, 25% max efficiency), class B (complementary push-pull, 78.5% max efficiency, crossover distortion), class AB (small idle bias eliminates crossover), and class D (PWM switching, 90%+ efficiency). Covers heat dissipation, efficiency derivation from the conduction angle, the complementary NPN/PNP output pair, and the class-D block diagram (modulator, H-bridge, LC reconstruction filter). Builds directly on the small-signal biasing and impedance work of amplifier-fundamentals.",
  "timeline": "Years 30-50",
  "outputs": [
    "power-amplifier-designs"
  ],
